WEBVTT

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.410
H-Huh?

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:07.720
Didn't I just come this way?

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.400
Just recently...

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.220
there was a burglary in a nearby town.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.070
It's not very safe here, so I suggest you be careful.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:22.490
If you ask me, hitchhiking's absolutely out of the question.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.090
Why are you trying to go home?

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:28.840
What?

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.950
Aren't you the Japanese person I'm seeing today?

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.180
Then that makes you...

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:38.830
I'm Billy Oliver, a sports psychologist.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.520
My work focuses on providing mental care for athletes.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.980
I'm actually quite busy,

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.590
but I made time for you as a favor to a friend, so why are you trying to go home?

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:52.940
Aren't you here because you have the yips?

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:54.740
Just let me off!

00:00:54.760 --> 00:01:00.410
I don't have any problems, and I definitely don't need any kind of bogus treatment.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.290
Now let me off, cyclone man!

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.540
Did you just say my treatment is bogus?

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.150
You seem to be well informed.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:09.790
You're right.

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:14.050
I only took this job because the Hornets will give me a ton of money if I cure you.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:17.130
Why else would I even consider dealing with an arrogant brat like you?

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:23.060
Hey!

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.350
You're going to break my transmission!

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.820
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.820
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:38.110
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:38.110
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:43.490
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:43.490
the only thing I truly have

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:48.790
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:48.790
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:54.130
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:54.130
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:59.390
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:59.390
the season of the coming summer began.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:04.770
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:04.770
I had begun to understand many things

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:10.860
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:10.860
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:16.400
garakuta no yama kara

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:16.400
In the junk I've piled up,

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.490
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:20.490
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:25.790
hibike kono koe yo

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:25.790
Let my voice echo on.

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:32.040
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:32.040
Let my heart resonate.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:37.720
namida kareru made

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:37.720
Until my tears dry up,

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:42.760
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:42.760
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:48.100
namida hareru made

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:48.100
Until my tears clear away,

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:53.110
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:53.110
though I may lose my way,

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:56.940
egakikake no ima

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:56.940
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.440
kizamu

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:04.200
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:02:58.440 --> 00:02:59.740
akashi

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:04.200
kono te de

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:09.960
The Fruits of the Treatment

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:09.960
The Fruits of the Treatment

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.660
Where am I?

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.710
That bastard!

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:36.150
He just threw a fist at me out of nowhere!

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.480
Damn, where did he go, anyway?

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.760
Good morning.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.670
Are you okay?

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:45.620
I apologize for my husband's behavior.

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.040
I guess he just got a bit too excited and punched you.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:02.380
How is it?

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.310
I hope it suits your taste.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:07.120
A Japanese friend of mine taught me how to make it.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.560
I figured you haven't eaten in a while.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.370
No, it's good.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:14.030
It's really good!

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:15.610
Really? That's great.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.200
By the way, where's that old man—

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.160
I mean, your husband?

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.360
He's out working at the moment.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.990
He said he wouldn't be long and told me to show you this video.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:29.710
What's on this DVD?

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:32.710
If this lady wasn't so nice,

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.590
I would already be on my way home.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:47.050
This is that last game, when I couldn't even pitch for a whole inning.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.160
Ball.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.050
Ball four.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.250
Geez, what's the point of this video?

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:01.690
Does he have a grudge against me?

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.880
This is the game before that.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.030
Give me a break.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.620
Why do I have to watch something like—

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:22.380
What, you can't even bear to see five minutes of your failures?

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.500
Hey, what's your problem?!

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:27.400
If you can't even look at your own pitching,

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:29.920
your yips is more serious than I thought.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.900
Listen, Shigeno.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.600
Let me make one thing clear to you.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:40.310
Unless you accept your condition and face the yips head-on,

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.650
you won't ever be cured.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:45.120
I don't care what you think of me,

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.120
but unless you accept your illness and confront it,

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.990
even I can't help you cure your yips.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:56.080
The yips isn't an urban legend or a supernatural phenomenon.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:06:00.850
It's a reality that's hanging over you at this very moment.

00:06:02.710 --> 00:06:03.970
All right.

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:06.510
So tell me how I can cure it.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:17.020
I know I don't need to tell you, but this is from the World Cup final.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:27.740
The shock of losing this game probably caused your yips.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:31.030
You were perfectly fine in the exhibition games,

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:35.540
but in regular season games, you've consistently broken down in stressful situations.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:39.000
It's a typical type of the yips.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.580
I get it!

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:42.290
I already understand that!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.090
Just tell me how to cure it!

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.310
There's no pill that can fix the yips.

00:06:46.310 --> 00:06:51.350
More than half of the patients I've worked with never fully recovered,

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:52.890
and were forced to retire.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:56.820
If, however, you can put your faith in me,

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:58.680
I'll do all I can to help you.

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.350
We'll conquer the yips together.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.400
A hypnosis treatment?

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:09.550
We'll start with an hour today, and we'll repeat it several times starting tomorrow.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:10.970
Wait, are you serious?

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:13.980
Not to be rude, but I don't believe in this hypnosis stuff.

00:07:13.980 --> 00:07:16.580
I'm not dumb enough to be hypnotized either.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.920
Hypnosis treatment isn't like the hypnosis you see on T.V.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:21.640
It's not magic or some stupid trick.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.790
It's an actual method of treatment.

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:28.920
There's a positive image which gives you optimism,

00:07:29.650 --> 00:07:33.470
and there's a negative image which causes pessimism.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:41.100
The yips puts you into an extreme state of hypnosis, where that negative image takes control.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:45.660
I've looked into your background,

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:50.030
and it appears you're the type of guy who triumphs by being optimistic.

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:53.110
You've faced various hurdles and roadblocks,

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.220
and have done things the hard way when necessary,

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:00.540
but you're ambitious and confident enough to take on those challenges.

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:05.760
At first glance, however, you also look like a reckless idiot.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.250
Where did you get your information?

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:10.050
The problem is why someone like you got the yips.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:15.680
We can take our time and untangle this knot one step at a time.

00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:21.230
Now, relax your shoulders.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.350
Relax.

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:25.940
Close your eyes.

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:32.560
I'm going to ask you questions about the final game, and other times in the past,

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:34.980
so I'd like you to answer honestly.

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:38.450
If you don't want to answer a question, that's okay.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:47.980
How is Shigeno doing?

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:50.860
He's taking the treatment seriously now.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:53.490
Do you think you'll be able to cure his yips?

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:54.900
I'm not sure.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:56.780
I'm trying various methods,

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:59.700
but the cause of his yips is still unclear.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.990
Wasn't it caused by the loss in the World Cup final?

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:06.590
Well, that definitely triggered it,

00:10:06.590 --> 00:10:09.830
but when I analyzed his personality and history,

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:13.910
I don't think he's the type to be traumatized by something that trivial.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:19.090
On one hand, it was a game of baseball on the global level,

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:22.390
and it's understandable that a loss of that caliber might be traumatic,

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:28.060
but he's experienced tremendous defeats and setbacks before.

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.980
I'd like a little more time.

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:43.780
Hey!

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:46.280
I've been here for five days.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:49.740
How much longer is this going to take?

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:55.210
If I just laze about in the middle of nowhere, my pitching will get rusty!

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.930
Then you can go home now.

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:05.060
I think we should see how the treatment is going by seeing you in a real game.

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:09.970
After all, we won't know if it's working unless you play a game.

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:13.620
Here, take this.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.660
It's medicine that'll help you with the yips.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:18.830
It's most effective if you take one right before you start.

00:11:18.830 --> 00:11:20.000
What?

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.890
You should've told me you had these!

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:25.240
I'll update the Bats on what's happening.

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:28.840
If you can play well under stress, then my work here is done.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:30.660
Go give it your all.

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.110
Yeah.

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:43.300
Hey, when did they invent a pill for the yips?

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:47.390
They're just vitamins.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.580
We only have one out.

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:07.700
I guess it's time to use him.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.680
Attention, please.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:12.520
Pitcher, number 56:

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:15.770
Goro Shigeno!

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:26.080
We were waiting for you!

00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:27.800
Blow them away!

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:29.900
Will this be all right?

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:31.830
He just got back yesterday.

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:34.100
This is what Dr. Oliver wants us to do.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:38.040
In order to figure out how well Shigeno's doing with the yips,

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:40.940
he has to pitch in a stressful situation.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:45.910
Shigeno, pitch to contact!

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:49.620
Ball.

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:54.700
Calm down.

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:56.560
This is simple.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:58.710
Just remember how good you are.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:03.930
You have a strong heart that can withstand any situation,

00:13:03.930 --> 00:13:05.930
and skills that have been honed to support it!

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:09.640
Strike!

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:12.970
You'll continue to give up home runs and normal runs,

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:17.310
and you'll probably lose some important games too.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.730
But as a professional, you just need to win more than you lose.

00:13:20.220 --> 00:13:23.150
You just need to keep taking it one out at a time.

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:27.200
You can reach much greater heights.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:35.870
Out!

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:36.600
All right!

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:37.710
A double play!

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.350
Strike out!

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.670
Game over!

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:57.850
All right!

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:01.480
Nice relief pitching.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:03.150
You also didn't give up any walks.

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.820
It's a good thing you went to Dr. Oliver.

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:08.280
It's probably just the medicine he gave me.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:10.720
Medicine?

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:17.060
Easy win.

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:18.040
Yeah.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:19.210
Shigeno.

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.210
Oh, it's you guys!

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:22.540
It's been a while.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:26.090
We heard you came back to the Bats, so we were worried.

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.980
I told you he just came back to polish some things up.

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:31.760
Right?

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:33.430
Yeah.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:36.710
It's great to be able to watch you play again,

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:39.140
but you've left the Bats once already.

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:41.480
Go back to the majors and win big.

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:45.650
We'll still cheer you on all the way while you're here, so don't you worry.

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:46.930
Thanks.

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:58.770
Honestly, I don't mind playing for the Bats forever.

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:00.120
You idiot!

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:03.170
If you say that again, I'll kick you off the Bats!

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:04.340
K-Kelloge.

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:08.270
Everyone here is aiming to rise to the majors.

00:15:08.270 --> 00:15:12.060
How can you care so little about it when you got there before us?

00:15:36.920 --> 00:15:37.740
Strike out!

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:40.210
"Another good game relieved by Shigeno.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:43.790
He'll be leading off for the next game."

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:44.630
Hear that?

00:15:44.630 --> 00:15:47.160
He's quite the guy, I tell you.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.020
He got over his yips in no time.

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:50.550
I wouldn't be so sure about that.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:55.830
He's playing in the minors, and those situations haven't been very stressful.

00:15:56.750 --> 00:15:58.270
Something's still not quite right.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:01.230
I can't put my finger on it,

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:05.770
but he's still not the Shigeno I knew.

00:16:05.770 --> 00:16:07.440
Wh-What?

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:12.360
Out!

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:20.140
Shigeno's pitched six innings with five hits and no runs and should be back in the majors in no time.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:22.210
Well, that's good news.

00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:24.790
I guess your vitamin pills are working.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.840
No, I haven't given him any more.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:28.970
He's doing well for now.

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.930
The treatment seems to have gone well,

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:41.720
but I don't think I can say he's fully recovered.

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:46.350
If that little bit of treatment was all he needed,

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:49.190
he could've cured it on his own.

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:57.990
I'm going back to the majors?!

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:01.360
The manager of the Hornets gave me a call this morning.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:05.540
If you do well in today's game, he wants you back immediately.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:07.830
All right!

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:07.830
However,

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:13.460
you must pitch at least seven innings with no runs or walks as the starting pitcher.

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:15.090
Not so easy, is it?

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:18.970
Not a problem.

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:25.560
If I can't pitch under that kind of pressure, I can't say I've conquered the yips.

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:30.480
No runs or walks through seven innings, huh?

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.710
It sure will be a challenge,

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:35.360
but considering how weak the Sharks' batters are, you'll be fine.

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:37.780
But be careful of one person.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:42.330
The third batter in their lineup is Silva, a major leaguer.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.120
Wh-Why is he here?

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:47.600
He's been in the minors for two weeks to recover from an injury,

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:50.300
but his injury's probably healed if he can play today. 

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:51.800
After this game, he's going back to the majors.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:53.300
Watch out for him.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.130
Play ball!

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:01.510
Strike out!

00:18:03.190 --> 00:18:04.470
Strike out!

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:12.000
Now hitting, number 52:

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.010
Silva!

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:23.370
Who would've thought we'd ever be back in the minors?

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:24.600
Damn.

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:27.890
I never thought I'd have to pitch against Silva at this level.

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:31.270
He's perfect for my final rehab game, I guess.

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:36.210
I'm confident since I struck him out last time, though.

00:18:37.700 --> 00:18:38.760
Strike!

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:41.550
Strike two.

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:49.350
You seem to be here because of a slump, but your speed and control haven't changed at all.

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:53.270
My eyes aren't used to this after such a long break.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.490
Strike out!

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:06.910
Damn, a forkball?

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:14.730
Shigeno's fully recovered.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:16.580
There's nothing to worry about now.

00:19:16.580 --> 00:19:18.090
It's his hat.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:23.150
I was wondering what was different, but his hat doesn't fly off when he pitches anymore.

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:25.390
Maybe that's why his pitching looked a little strange.

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:26.560
His hat?

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:30.080
Oh right, his hat used to fly off after every pitch.

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:32.600
I'm sure it's just a smaller hat now.

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:35.690
I sure hope you're right.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:39.990
I told him once that he should get it fixed.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:45.910
There's no point in him wasting energy picking up his hat after every pitch.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.180
Oh.

00:19:47.180 --> 00:19:50.960
Then he probably took your advice and switched to a smaller size.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:54.100
But he said something interesting to me...

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:55.860
"I don't mind it falling off.

00:19:55.860 --> 00:20:02.050
When my hat falls off, I know I'm pitching well."

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:33.810
This is odd.

00:20:33.810 --> 00:20:35.120
All right!

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:37.260
Silva can't even touch his pitches.

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:40.510
Yeah, he'll be back to the majors in no time.

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:41.910
But still...

00:20:41.910 --> 00:20:43.220
Is something wrong, Peter?

00:20:43.220 --> 00:20:46.140
N-No, not really.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:51.890
Keep it up.

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:54.440
Just two more innings until you can go back to the majors.

00:20:56.170 --> 00:21:00.230
I can't even imagine giving up a hit anymore.

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:04.110
I just need to remember to stay calm as I pitch!

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:05.910
Strike!

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:09.860
His pitches are over 90 mph and are consistently strikes.

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:13.190
Once the count is against him, he throws in a fork.

00:21:13.190 --> 00:21:15.920
Our lineup doesn't stand a chance.

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:23.260
Safe!

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:28.050
Oh, man.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:33.930
Out!

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:37.580
This is nothing to worry about.

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:40.750
Now hitting, number 52:

00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:45.880
Silva!

00:21:51.970 --> 00:21:56.210
No matter who's batting, I just need to pitch to the corners.

00:21:56.690 --> 00:21:57.670
That's all I need to do!

00:21:58.690 --> 00:21:59.630
Strike!

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:05.490
His pitches are all fast pitches to the corners.

00:22:05.490 --> 00:22:09.800
Still, he's not the same as he was in the World Cup.

00:22:12.440 --> 00:22:13.260
Ball.

00:22:14.850 --> 00:22:17.270
Am I getting used to his pitching?

00:22:17.910 --> 00:22:19.940
No, that's not it.

00:22:20.470 --> 00:22:24.540
When I struck out at the World Cup, I was overwhelmed by devastation.

00:22:24.540 --> 00:22:27.110
He doesn't have that overwhelming presence anymore.

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:59.060
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:59.100
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:59.060 --> 00:23:04.440
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:04.480
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:10.700
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:10.740
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:15.490
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:15.540
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:16.310 --> 00:23:22.190
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:16.310 --> 00:23:22.190
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:28.030
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:28.030
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:28.030 --> 00:23:33.870
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:28.030 --> 00:23:33.870
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:39.290
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:33.870 --> 00:23:39.290
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:39.290 --> 00:23:45.750
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:39.290 --> 00:23:45.750
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:51.010
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:54.470
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:51.010 --> 00:23:54.470
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.470 --> 00:23:56.930
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.470 --> 00:24:03.310
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:56.930 --> 00:24:03.310
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:07.090
sotto

00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:07.090
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:15.300
Preview

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:15.300
Preview

00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:12.760
What's wrong with me?

00:24:12.760 --> 00:24:17.010
I can't bring my "A" game in a one-on-one match anymore!

00:24:17.420 --> 00:24:21.560
Am I really cured of the yips, Dr. Oliver?!

00:24:21.560 --> 00:24:25.000
Next time, on Major: What it Takes to be a Pro.

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:28.930
Next Time

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:28.930
Next Time

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:28.930
What it Takes to be a Pro

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:28.930
What it Takes to be a Pro

00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:27.270
Run toward the stage of your dreams!
